{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>When you bring a new meal-offering.</b> The bread of waving is the principal, and with it seven lambs, one bull of the herd, two rams, and two lambs of well-being. And the burnt-offering mentioned in this passage is the obligation of the day. The proof for their words is that regarding Shabbat and the Festival he did not explain anything at all; he only mentioned the Festival of Unleavened Bread, Tabernacles, and the Day of Atonement, [saying] 'their offerings, an offering by fire to YHWH,' but did not state how many. And likewise on the Day of Trumpeting he did not mention the new-moon burnt-offering and the regular burnt-offering and its meal-offering — it is the first burnt-offering."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:48.025112943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}